meta {
  name: ENG - register iTwin A
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/eng/twins
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "iTwinId": "{{twinA}}",
    "code": "PLANT-A",
    "name": "Plant A",
    "description": "First plant, for the isolation check."
  }
}

docs {
  Registering a twin is optional: naming an unknown one on a write creates it.
  It is done explicitly here so the twin carries a readable code and name rather
  than defaulting to its own UUID.

  Idempotent. Re-running returns the existing row rather than failing, so the
  isolation sequence can be replayed without a reset.
}
